  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Summary",
      "html": "<p>Greek has twenty-four letters. Most look like their Latin cousins, but some do not sound the way they look (η is a long e, ρ is r, χ is ch as in Scottish loch). Learn each letter&#x27;s small form, its capital, its name and its sound, in order, so you can find words in a lexicon.</p>"
    },
